/**
 * Stock transfer workflow (issue #62, Process A).
 *
 *   create/submit indent ──► approve ──► dispatch ──► receive (per STN)
 *                              │    ▲       │            │
 *                              ▼    │       ▼            ▼
 *                        picking list   STN, cases,     MRN generated by
 *                        stock reserved packing list,   the receiving branch,
 *                        back orders ───┘ stock deducted  stock posted
 *                        (picked again   once
 *                         as stock arrives)
 *
 * As at CPD, an indent can ship over several STNs, one STN can carry several indents of
 * the same branch, and CPD can send a direct STN with no indent at all.
 *
 * Goods are in transit on the STN. Transfers never create an MIT: MIT is only for Mobis
 * invoices. The receiving branch generates an MRN (one per receipt when received in parts).
 *
 * Each action runs in one database transaction. Status changes are claimed
 * with a conditional update and stock rows are locked with SELECT ... FOR
 * UPDATE, so a double click or two users acting at once can never deduct or
 * post stock twice. Notifications are sent after the transaction commits.
 */
